+**Append-only time-series tables** (samples, results, logs) take
+`default=uuid.uuid7` for their `id` (time-ordered keys keep the primary-key
+index compact; every other table keeps `uuid.uuid4`, and a secret is never
+an id — tokens are separate hashed columns). Give the time column a BRIN
+index (`Index(..., postgresql_using="brin")`) next to the usual
+`(owner_id, time)` B-tree, and purge old rows with
+`app.tasks.jobs._delete_in_batches` rather than one `DELETE`.
+
