+- Every retention purge deletes in batches of 5 000 rows, each its own
+  transaction (since 0.127.0), so a first purge after shortening retention
+  never holds one huge lock. The sample tables have BRIN indexes on their
+  time column and time-ordered UUIDv7 keys for new rows.
 
